{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:20707-1","published":"2026-03-06T11:53:41Z","modified":"2026-03-23T04:53:09.014684Z","related":["CVE-2025-10911","CVE-2025-8732","CVE-2026-0989","CVE-2026-0990","CVE-2026-0992","CVE-2026-1757"],"upstream":["CVE-2025-10911","CVE-2025-8732","CVE-2026-0989","CVE-2026-0990","CVE-2026-0992","CVE-2026-1757"],"summary":"Security update for libxslt, libxml2","details":"This update for libxslt, libxml2 fixes the following issues:\n\nChanges in libxml2:\n\n- CVE-2026-0990: call stack overflow may lead to application crash due to infinite recursion in\n  `xmlCatalogXMLResolveURI` (bsc#1256807, bsc#1256811).\n- CVE-2026-0992: excessive resource consumption when processing XML catalogs due to exponential behavior when handling\n  `nextCatalog` elements (bsc#1256809, bsc#1256812).\n- CVE-2025-8732: infinite recursion in catalog parsing functions when processing malformed SGML catalog files\n  (bsc#1247858).\n- CVE-2026-1757: memory leak in the `xmllint` interactive shell (bsc#1257594, bsc#1257595).\n- CVE-2025-10911: parsing xsl nodes may lead to use-after-free with key data stored cross-RVT (bsc#1250553).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libxml2","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Micro 6.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/libxml2&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Micro%206.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.11.6-12.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libexslt0":"1.1.38-8.1","libxml2-2":"2.11.6-12.1","libxml2-tools":"2.11.6-12.1","libxslt1":"1.1.38-8.1","python311-libxml2":"2.11.6-12.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:20707-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"libxml2-python","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Micro 6.0","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/libxml2-python&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Micro%206.0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"2.11.6-12.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"libexslt0":"1.1.38-8.1","libxml2-2":"2.11.6-12.1","libxml2-tools":